{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W93VGEHn4avSo8tfms9R1V","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# WI-274 — dev-setup stale-venv recovery + single-home coordinator dials\n2\t\n3\t**WI:** WI-274 · **Status:** queued · **Delivers:** SR-032 (part A), SR-026 (part B)\n4\t\n5\tTwo dev-environment ergonomics gaps, filed together (owner directive\n6\t2026-07-23): both are \"the declared value lives in the wrong number of places\"\n7\tproblems surfaced by the same day's hands-on work.\n8\t\n9\t## Part A — dev-setup cannot recover a stale `.venv`\n10\t\n11\t### Problem\n12\t\n13\t`scripts/dev-setup.{ps1,sh}` cannot bring an existing sub-3.11 `.venv` to the\n14\tPython 3.11 floor the repo now declares (WI-262/WI-270) — the environment the\n15\tdeclared test command actually runs through. Three verified gaps\n16\t(meta-repo dev box, 2026-07-23: `.venv` = Python **3.8.10**, Python **3.12**\n17\tinstalled and listed by `py -0p`):\n18\t\n19\t1. **No recovery path.** `-Install`/`--install` fail closed on a sub-3.11\n20\t   `.venv`: *\"move or remove that environment, then rerun\"*\n21\t   (`scripts/dev-setup.ps1` ~line 135, `scripts/dev-setup.sh` ~line 150).\n22\t   Consent-first is right, but no *consented* recreate is ever offered — manual\n23\t   deletion is the only way forward.\n24\t2. **`-Check` never names the stale venv.** `$venvSupported` (ps1) / the `PY`\n25\t   probe (sh) silently fall back to the ambient interpreter; the report\n26\t   describes *that* environment with no line saying `.venv` exists but is below\n27\t   the floor. The one signal a contributor gets is misleading\n28\t   (`[missing] runtime (python) — install Python 3.11+`).\n29\t3. **Discovery is shadowed by the stale venv itself.** The candidate list\n30\t   (`py`, `python`, `python3`) never tries version-pinned forms, so when the\n31\t   stale venv is active / first on PATH (VS Code auto-activation — exactly\n32\t   where a contributor runs dev-setup), **every** candidate resolves to the\n33\t   venv's 3.8 and `-Install` dies with *\"Python 3.11+ not found on PATH\"* even\n34\t   though 3.12 is installed (`py -3.12` works). Verified live.\n35\t\n36\tNet: SR-032's AC (\"the scaffolded onboard/dev-setup scripts run to a green\n37\tsetup\") is unmet whenever a pre-floor `.venv` exists. The kit-shipped\n38\t`project-trajectory/scripts/setup.{ps1,sh}` carry the same fail-closed\n39\t\"move or remove\" pattern (setup.ps1:37 / setup.sh:29) — whether the fix ships\n40\tdownstream is a **deliberate decision in this WI** (downstream migration\n41\tsurface; flag, don't silently drift — `tests/test_dogfood_sync.py`).\n42\t\n43\t### Approach\n44\t\n45\tSmallest change preserving the consent-first posture, in both scripts\n46\t(behavior parity, per-script idiom):\n47\t\n48\t- **(a) Consented recreate.** On `-Install`/`--install` with a sub-3.11\n49\t  `.venv`: offer `Recreate ./.venv with <interpreter> (Python <ver>)? [y/N]` —\n50\t  on yes, remove the old venv, `venv` afresh with the discovered 3.11+\n51\t  interpreter, then the pinned `requirements-dev.txt` install (same path as\n52\t  the fresh-create branch). Decline keeps today's fail-closed message and\n53\t  exit 1. Non-interactive `read` failure declines gracefully (the existing\n54\t  `offer_cli` pattern).\n55\t- **(b) Explicit stale report.** `-Check`/`--check` emit a dedicated line when\n56\t  `.venv` exists below the floor (e.g. `[stale] .venv is Python 3.8.10 —\n57\t  below the 3.11 floor; rerun -Install to recreate it`) instead of silently\n58\t  describing the ambient interpreter.\n59\t- **(c) Version-pinned discovery.** Append pinned candidates after the bare\n60\t  ones: Windows `py -3.13`/`py -3.12`/`py -3.11` (each still floor-checked);\n61\t  POSIX `python3.13`/`python3.12`/`python3.11`. A stale venv on PATH can then\n62\t  never hide an installed 3.11+ from the recreate offer.\n63\t- **Tests** in `tests/test_onboard_devsetup.py`, following its existing\n64\t  patterns (the 3.11-floor text assertion is already there): recreate offer\n65\t  present in both scripts, stale-venv report line present, pinned candidates\n66\t  probed, decline path stays fail-closed.\n67\t- **Downstream call:** decide + record whether `setup.{ps1,sh}` (scaffold-time,\n68\t  where a pre-existing `.venv` is far rarer) get the same offer; default\n69\t  conservative — meta-repo `dev-setup` only, with the decision noted in the\n70\t  close deliverable.\n71\t\n72\t## Part B — coordinator dials declared once, not per launcher\n73\t\n74\t### Problem\n75\t\n76\t`AGENT_JOBS`, the fallback `AGENT_MODEL`/`AGENT_MODEL_MAP`, and the\n77\t`AGENT_CMD*` templates are declared as env slots in **each** launcher:\n78\t`agent-resume.cmd`, `agent-resume.sh`, and (`AGENT_JOBS` only)\n79\t`agent-resume.command`. A one-dial owner change therefore edits the same value\n80\tin up to three files — the 2026-07-22 dial turn (Fable→Opus strong + serial\n81\tdefault) touched exactly this surface. The duplication is *not* inherent: the\n82\tper-platform launchers must exist (cmd can't source sh; double-click entry\n83\tpoints), but the **values** live there only because env slots were the original\n84\tconfig mechanism. The repo has already escaped this twice:\n85\t\n86\t- model **routing** moved to `docs/agents.csv` + `docs/agents-enabled` (the\n87\t  env maps are now the declared legacy *fallback*);\n88\t- the `run.*` launchers are thin because `run_menu.py` reads\n89\t  `docs/stack.ini [run]` (IF-048/IF-049);\n90\t- `subagent_gate` reads a declared file **with a launcher env override**\n91\t  (IF-038) — the precedence pattern part B needs.\n92\t\n93\t### Approach\n94\t\n95\tLet the destination read the dials: `agent_loop.py` (or `agent_common`, where\n96\tthe declared-surface reads already live — IF-065) reads a declared config\n97\tsection at boot — **IF-068 (Proposed**, filed with this WI**)** — with\n98\tprecedence **CLI flag > `AGENT_*` env > declared file > built-in default**.\n99\tThe env slots keep working (nothing breaks, the L-22 inherited-value fix stays\n100\thonored); the launchers shrink to platform plumbing (consent banner, `cd`,\n101\texec) plus a comment pointing at the declared home; the `.command` `AGENT_JOBS`\n102\tslot can drop entirely.\n103\t\n104\tDesign calls left to the build session (recorded in IF-068's notes):\n105\t\n106\t- **Home:** an `[agent-loop]` section in the existing `docs/stack.ini` (one\n107\t  declared-config home, IF-049 precedent) vs a sibling declared file next to\n108\t  `docs/agents-enabled`. Lean stack.ini — one fewer file, same parser.\n109\t- **Scope of migration:** move `AGENT_JOBS` + the fallback model dials first;\n110\t  the `AGENT_CMD*` templates may stay launcher-side (they are genuinely\n111\t  per-platform strings).\n112\t- **Downstream:** the launchers + `agent_loop.py` ship as templates — the same\n113\t  change lands in `project-trajectory/scripts/agent-resume.template.*` (or is\n114\t  deliberately deferred with the reason recorded); migration note either way.\n115\t\n116\t**Trade-off accepted:** a double-clicking user no longer sees the dials in the\n117\tfile they clicked — mitigated by the launcher comment naming the declared home.\n118\tOverhead is modest (stdlib `configparser`, one precedence rule, tests) against\n119\ta recurring three-file edit for every dial turn.\n120\t\n121\t## Interfaces\n122\t\n123\t- Part A: no cross-module seam — acts only within `scripts/dev-setup.{ps1,sh}`\n124\t  and their tests (the optional downstream decision touches\n125\t  `project-trajectory/scripts/setup.{ps1,sh}`, the same onboarding module).\n126\t- Part B: `IF-015` (existing) — the agent_loop CLI seam `--jobs` already rides;\n127\t  `IF-068` (**Proposed**, filed at this filing) — the new declared-config read;\n128\t  nearest existing `IF-049`, insufficient because that seam belongs to\n129\t  run_menu's capability menu, not the coordinator's dials.\n130\t\n131\t## Done-when\n132\t\n133\t- [ ] **A:** both dev-setup scripts offer the consented recreate; decline keeps\n134\t      the fail-closed exit; behavior parity ps1 ↔ sh.\n135\t- [ ] **A:** `-Check`/`--check` name a stale `.venv` explicitly.\n136\t- [ ] **A:** pinned-interpreter discovery lands; a venv-activated shell with a\n137\t      newer CPython installed reaches the recreate offer (the 2026-07-23 repro).\n138\t- [ ] **A:** downstream (`setup.{ps1,sh}`) decision made and recorded in the\n139\t      Deliverable.\n140\t- [ ] **B:** the declared dial home exists and `agent_loop` reads it with the\n141\t      documented precedence; launchers carry no duplicated dial values;\n142\t      IF-068 flipped Proposed → Stable (or the row updated to the shape built).\n143\t- [ ] **B:** template/downstream disposition decided and recorded (migration\n144\t      note if shipped).\n145\t- [ ] New behavior covered in `tests/` (dev-setup: `test_onboard_devsetup.py`;\n146\t      dials: the agent_loop/launcher test homes); commit bar green\n147\t      (`pytest -q -n auto -m smoke` + `check_docs.py`).\n148\t- [ ] Row set `done` (Deliverable filled, SpecRef cleared); spec archived to\n149\t      `docs/archive/specs/` with close date.\n150\t\n151\t## Notes / open questions\n152\t\n153\t- The meta-repo's own `.venv` is the live part-A repro **and is now broken\n154\t  outright**: its base CPython 3.8 was uninstalled on 2026-07-23 (Python 3.11\n155\t  installed in its place), so the venv must be recreated before *any* local\n156\t  test run — the first act of the next session, and exactly the walk part A\n157\t  automates. `tests/__pycache__/*.cpython-38*` debris should be cleared with it.\n158\t- Part B intersects the owner's uncommitted 2026-07-22 launcher dial change\n159\t  (Fable→Opus strong / serial default) — build part B **after** that lands so\n160\t  the migration moves the *current* declared values.\n161\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3999ba4b-9a04-4264-9bca-08ca733e1022","uuid":"35b7159f-46a6-468e-9f8f-e9daa620c7ca","timestamp":"2026-07-23T13:06:56.688Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\1-g3-WI-274-0083\\docs\\specs\\WI-274.md","content":"# WI-274 — dev-setup stale-venv recovery + single-home coordinator dials\n\n**WI:** WI-274 · **Status:** queued · **Delivers:** SR-032 (part A), SR-026 (part B)\n\nTwo dev-environment ergonomics gaps, filed together (owner directive\n2026-07-23): both are \"the declared value lives in the wrong number of places\"\nproblems surfaced by the same day's hands-on work.\n\n## Part A — dev-setup cannot recover a stale `.venv`\n\n### Problem\n\n`scripts/dev-setup.{ps1,sh}` cannot bring an existing sub-3.11 `.venv` to the\nPython 3.11 floor the repo now declares (WI-262/WI-270) — the environment the\ndeclared test command actually runs through. Three verified gaps\n(meta-repo dev box, 2026-07-23: `.venv` = Python **3.8.10**, Python **3.12**\ninstalled and listed by `py -0p`):\n\n1. **No recovery path.** `-Install`/`--install` fail closed on a sub-3.11\n   `.venv`: *\"move or remove that environment, then rerun\"*\n   (`scripts/dev-setup.ps1` ~line 135, `scripts/dev-setup.sh` ~line 150).\n   Consent-first is right, but no *consented* recreate is ever offered — manual\n   deletion is the only way forward.\n2. **`-Check` never names the stale venv.** `$venvSupported` (ps1) / the `PY`\n   probe (sh) silently fall back to the ambient interpreter; the report\n   describes *that* environment with no line saying `.venv` exists but is below\n   the floor. The one signal a contributor gets is misleading\n   (`[missing] runtime (python) — install Python 3.11+`).\n3. **Discovery is shadowed by the stale venv itself.** The candidate list\n   (`py`, `python`, `python3`) never tries version-pinned forms, so when the\n   stale venv is active / first on PATH (VS Code auto-activation — exactly\n   where a contributor runs dev-setup), **every** candidate resolves to the\n   venv's 3.8 and `-Install` dies with *\"Python 3.11+ not found on PATH\"* even\n   though 3.12 is installed (`py -3.12` works). Verified live.\n\nNet: SR-032's AC (\"the scaffolded onboard/dev-setup scripts run to a green\nsetup\") is unmet whenever a pre-floor `.venv` exists. The kit-shipped\n`project-trajectory/scripts/setup.{ps1,sh}` carry the same fail-closed\n\"move or remove\" pattern (setup.ps1:37 / setup.sh:29) — whether the fix ships\ndownstream is a **deliberate decision in this WI** (downstream migration\nsurface; flag, don't silently drift — `tests/test_dogfood_sync.py`).\n\n### Approach\n\nSmallest change preserving the consent-first posture, in both scripts\n(behavior parity, per-script idiom):\n\n- **(a) Consented recreate.** On `-Install`/`--install` with a sub-3.11\n  `.venv`: offer `Recreate ./.venv with <interpreter> (Python <ver>)? [y/N]` —\n  on yes, remove the old venv, `venv` afresh with the discovered 3.11+\n  interpreter, then the pinned `requirements-dev.txt` install (same path as\n  the fresh-create branch). Decline keeps today's fail-closed message and\n  exit 1. Non-interactive `read` failure declines gracefully (the existing\n  `offer_cli` pattern).\n- **(b) Explicit stale report.** `-Check`/`--check` emit a dedicated line when\n  `.venv` exists below the floor (e.g. `[stale] .venv is Python 3.8.10 —\n  below the 3.11 floor; rerun -Install to recreate it`) instead of silently\n  describing the ambient interpreter.\n- **(c) Version-pinned discovery.** Append pinned candidates after the bare\n  ones: Windows `py -3.13`/`py -3.12`/`py -3.11` (each still floor-checked);\n  POSIX `python3.13`/`python3.12`/`python3.11`. A stale venv on PATH can then\n  never hide an installed 3.11+ from the recreate offer.\n- **Tests** in `tests/test_onboard_devsetup.py`, following its existing\n  patterns (the 3.11-floor text assertion is already there): recreate offer\n  present in both scripts, stale-venv report line present, pinned candidates\n  probed, decline path stays fail-closed.\n- **Downstream call:** decide + record whether `setup.{ps1,sh}` (scaffold-time,\n  where a pre-existing `.venv` is far rarer) get the same offer; default\n  conservative — meta-repo `dev-setup` only, with the decision noted in the\n  close deliverable.\n\n## Part B — coordinator dials declared once, not per launcher\n\n### Problem\n\n`AGENT_JOBS`, the fallback `AGENT_MODEL`/`AGENT_MODEL_MAP`, and the\n`AGENT_CMD*` templates are declared as env slots in **each** launcher:\n`agent-resume.cmd`, `agent-resume.sh`, and (`AGENT_JOBS` only)\n`agent-resume.command`. A one-dial owner change therefore edits the same value\nin up to three files — the 2026-07-22 dial turn (Fable→Opus strong + serial\ndefault) touched exactly this surface. The duplication is *not* inherent: the\nper-platform launchers must exist (cmd can't source sh; double-click entry\npoints), but the **values** live there only because env slots were the original\nconfig mechanism. The repo has already escaped this twice:\n\n- model **routing** moved to `docs/agents.csv` + `docs/agents-enabled` (the\n  env maps are now the declared legacy *fallback*);\n- the `run.*` launchers are thin because `run_menu.py` reads\n  `docs/stack.ini [run]` (IF-048/IF-049);\n- `subagent_gate` reads a declared file **with a launcher env override**\n  (IF-038) — the precedence pattern part B needs.\n\n### Approach\n\nLet the destination read the dials: `agent_loop.py` (or `agent_common`, where\nthe declared-surface reads already live — IF-065) reads a declared config\nsection at boot — **IF-068 (Proposed**, filed with this WI**)** — with\nprecedence **CLI flag > `AGENT_*` env > declared file > built-in default**.\nThe env slots keep working (nothing breaks, the L-22 inherited-value fix stays\nhonored); the launchers shrink to platform plumbing (consent banner, `cd`,\nexec) plus a comment pointing at the declared home; the `.command` `AGENT_JOBS`\nslot can drop entirely.\n\nDesign calls left to the build session (recorded in IF-068's notes):\n\n- **Home:** an `[agent-loop]` section in the existing `docs/stack.ini` (one\n  declared-config home, IF-049 precedent) vs a sibling declared file next to\n  `docs/agents-enabled`. Lean stack.ini — one fewer file, same parser.\n- **Scope of migration:** move `AGENT_JOBS` + the fallback model dials first;\n  the `AGENT_CMD*` templates may stay launcher-side (they are genuinely\n  per-platform strings).\n- **Downstream:** the launchers + `agent_loop.py` ship as templates — the same\n  change lands in `project-trajectory/scripts/agent-resume.template.*` (or is\n  deliberately deferred with the reason recorded); migration note either way.\n\n**Trade-off accepted:** a double-clicking user no longer sees the dials in the\nfile they clicked — mitigated by the launcher comment naming the declared home.\nOverhead is modest (stdlib `configparser`, one precedence rule, tests) against\na recurring three-file edit for every dial turn.\n\n## Interfaces\n\n- Part A: no cross-module seam — acts only within `scripts/dev-setup.{ps1,sh}`\n  and their tests (the optional downstream decision touches\n  `project-trajectory/scripts/setup.{ps1,sh}`, the same onboarding module).\n- Part B: `IF-015` (existing) — the agent_loop CLI seam `--jobs` already rides;\n  `IF-068` (**Proposed**, filed at this filing) — the new declared-config read;\n  nearest existing `IF-049`, insufficient because that seam belongs to\n  run_menu's capability menu, not the coordinator's dials.\n\n## Done-when\n\n- [ ] **A:** both dev-setup scripts offer the consented recreate; decline keeps\n      the fail-closed exit; behavior parity ps1 ↔ sh.\n- [ ] **A:** `-Check`/`--check` name a stale `.venv` explicitly.\n- [ ] **A:** pinned-interpreter discovery lands; a venv-activated shell with a\n      newer CPython installed reaches the recreate offer (the 2026-07-23 repro).\n- [ ] **A:** downstream (`setup.{ps1,sh}`) decision made and recorded in the\n      Deliverable.\n- [ ] **B:** the declared dial home exists and `agent_loop` reads it with the\n      documented precedence; launchers carry no duplicated dial values;\n      IF-068 flipped Proposed → Stable (or the row updated to the shape built).\n- [ ] **B:** template/downstream disposition decided and recorded (migration\n      note if shipped).\n- [ ] New behavior covered in `tests/` (dev-setup: `test_onboard_devsetup.py`;\n      dials: the agent_loop/launcher test homes); commit bar green\n      (`pytest -q -n auto -m smoke` + `check_docs.py`).\n- [ ] Row set `done` (Deliverable filled, SpecRef cleared); spec archived to\n      `docs/archive/specs/` with close date.\n\n## Notes / open questions\n\n- The meta-repo's own `.venv` is the live part-A repro **and is now broken\n  outright**: its base CPython 3.8 was uninstalled on 2026-07-23 (Python 3.11\n  installed in its place), so the venv must be recreated before *any* local\n  test run — the first act of the next session, and exactly the walk part A\n  automates. `tests/__pycache__/*.cpython-38*` debris should be cleared with it.\n- Part B intersects the owner's uncommitted 2026-07-22 launcher dial change\n  (Fable→Opus strong / serial default) — build part B **after** that lands so\n  the migration moves the *current* declared values.\n","numLines":161,"startLine":1,"totalLines":161}}}
