{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdK5mkUM8bi8ZRyUfD5U3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both MAJOR findings from `002-REVIEW-A` are addressed and committed (`6c1c63d`), with the required `WI:`/`Train:`/`Base:` trailers and a clean tree.\n\n## What I fixed\n\n**[A] `dev-setup.ps1` broken-`.venv` detection** (the reviewer's live repro)\n- **Root cause:** `$venvExists` keyed off `.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe`, so a broken/empty `.venv` *directory* (base CPython uninstalled, or an empty leftover) slipped past the recreate branch — `-Install` took the ordinary create prompt, skipped `venv` (dir already there), and crashed at the pip line.\n- **Fix:** `$venvDirExists = Test-Path \".venv\" -PathType Container` detects the directory independently, so broken **and** sub-floor venvs route through the same consented recreate — parity with `dev-setup.sh`'s existing `[ -d .venv ]` gate. Messages now distinguish `unusable (no working interpreter)` from a named sub-floor version; aligned `dev-setup.sh` wording for the broken case.\n- **Regression:** added `test_meta_devsetup_ps1_broken_venv_offers_recreate` (Windows-gated, behavioral). I reproduced the pre-fix crash, then verified the fix live on **pwsh 7 and Windows PowerShell 5.1**: pre-fix exits 0 with no detection; post-fix reports `[stale] unusable`, offers the recreate, and stays fail-closed on decline (exit 1, venv preserved). Also confirmed a *healthy* venv is not falsely flagged.\n\n**[B] Launcher-template dial disposition** (was undecided/unrecorded)\n- **Decision (recorded in spec Part B): DEFER** the launcher-template migration. A fresh scaffold ships placeholder dials it fills once and rarely turns, so the single-home only pays off for a heavy dial-turner (this meta-repo); IF-068 is fail-soft, so nothing breaks.\n- Shipped the **capability** regardless (`agent_loop` reads `docs/stack.ini [agent-loop]`) plus **in-place migration guidance**: `stack.ini.template`'s `[agent-loop]` reframed as the opt-in single home + a pointer comment by each launcher template's `AGENT_JOBS` slot. `.command` template needs no change (pure delegator).\n\n## Verification\n- Directly-affected suites green: `test_onboard_devsetup` + `test_agent_loop` + `test_dogfood_sync` (**160 passed**).\n- Full suite: **1379 passed, 7 skipped, 1 failed**. The one red — `test_forward_only_unit_over_the_real_meta_repo` — is **pre-existing and out of worker scope**: it reads `docs/status.md` + the `done` WI-275 registry row (neither in my diff; a worker may not edit `status.md`). The prior build commit `803265d` recorded the identical exclusion; it's the integrator's to resolve.\n- `check_docs.py`: OK (0 broken). Pre-commit freshness/integrity floor: all steps **PASS**.\n\nThe iteration/telemetry log is written by the dispatcher (`agent_loop`) around this session, so I didn't hand-author one. The WI is ready for re-review."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1072,"cache_read_input_tokens":217135,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1072},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3999ba4b-9a04-4264-9bca-08ca733e1022","uuid":"34b567a7-fc10-4f61-83d0-0e4a4e80b427","request_id":"req_011CdK5mieU2Huc7dwxXjgLK"}
